result: 'docs/caps.md written. Decided: caps are their OWN pass (not merged with errset),
  sharing only the SCC fixpoint utility. `needs` clause (twin of `! E`) at fn/method/class/module
  sites, inferred-by-default + narrows. Closed lattice w/ scoped containment. CAP_SITES
  single-source table; missing runtime attribution = build error (Q7). Q1 resolved:
  promote iff cap row EMPTY (stricter than state-free, airtight). Q6 resolved: cap
  row part of function TYPE, propagates through HOFs/actors, no laundering. FFI taint
  one-directional, --deny enforced by undischargeable effect.'
description: 'Fully spec the capability system as its OWN pass, distinct from error-effects.
  Lattice + closed cap classes, path/resource scoping + containment, the four declaration
  sites (module/class/fn/method) with idiomatic inferred-by-default + annotation-narrows
  syntax, derivation pass (SCC fixpoint, separate from errset), primitive cap-attribution
  table (single source of truth like store_decorators.rs), caps on function TYPES
  (Q6 soundness), runtime cap-tagging as build-error-if-missing (Q7), and resolve
  Q1 (state-as-cap soundness: decide opt-in @promotable vs free). Output: docs/caps.md.'
